=== ansible/README.md
# Generated Ansible project

Nothing here has been run. Review it, then:

1. `ansible-galaxy collection install -r requirements.yml` (the collection version is pinned).
2. Fill in ansible_user and each ansible_host in inventory.yml; set KUBECONFIG for the control host.
3. Dry run: `ansible-playbook cgroupv2-migrate.yml --check --diff`.
4. Read-only checks: `ansible-playbook cgroupv2-migrate.yml --tags preflight`.
5. Migrate: the canary group runs first, one node at a time, and the play stops on the first failure.
6. Roll back a node: `ansible-playbook cgroupv2-rollback.yml --limit NODE`.

Kubernetes permissions: the identity in the kubeconfig needs, at least, get/list/patch on nodes, get/list on pods and create on pods/eviction
(that is what draining uses); check with kubectl auth can-i before running. The role marks nodes it cordons with the annotation
cgroupguard.io/migrating and uncordons only those.

Security: use SSH keys in an agent or SSM, keep secrets in Ansible Vault, give the connecting user a
least-privilege sudo rule, and keep kubeconfig output hidden (the role sets no_log on Kubernetes tasks).
=== ansible/ansible.cfg
[defaults]
inventory = inventory.yml
roles_path = roles
host_key_checking = True
retry_files_enabled = False

[ssh_connection]
pipelining = True
=== ansible/cgroupv2-migrate.yml
---
# Generated by cgroupguard. Review before use; nothing here has been run.
# Tags select tasks inside the role: preflight = read-only checks only (plus the read-only detection tasks,
# which always run), migrate = changes, verify = post-checks. Without --tags everything runs.
# Run the canary first, check it, then continue:
#   ansible-playbook cgroupv2-migrate.yml --check --diff     # dry run
#   ansible-playbook cgroupv2-migrate.yml --tags preflight   # read-only checks
#   ansible-playbook cgroupv2-migrate.yml                    # migrate (one node at a time)
# Authenticate with SSH keys in an agent or SSM, keep secrets in Ansible Vault, and use a
# least-privilege sudo rule. No secret is stored in these files.
- name: Migrate the canary node to cgroup v2
  hosts: cgroupv2_canary
  serial: 1
  any_errors_fatal: true
  max_fail_percentage: 0
  become: true
  gather_facts: true
  roles:
    - role: cgroupv2

- name: Wait for a human to confirm the canary
  hosts: localhost
  connection: local
  gather_facts: false
  tasks:
    - name: Pause until the canary node is verified and has soaked
      ansible.builtin.pause:
        prompt: Canary node migrated. Verify workloads and metrics, let it soak, then press Enter to continue or Ctrl-C to abort
      tags: [migrate]

- name: Migrate the remaining nodes to cgroup v2
  hosts: cgroupv2_rest
  serial: 1
  any_errors_fatal: true
  max_fail_percentage: 0
  become: true
  gather_facts: true
  roles:
    - role: cgroupv2
=== ansible/cgroupv2-rollback.yml
---
# Generated by cgroupguard. Restores the backups taken by the migration on the hosts you target.
# Limit it: ansible-playbook cgroupv2-rollback.yml --limit NODE
# After it finishes, verify the node and uncordon it yourself.
- name: Roll the cgroup v2 migration back on the selected nodes
  hosts: cgroupv2_canary:cgroupv2_rest
  serial: 1
  any_errors_fatal: true
  become: true
  gather_facts: true
  tasks:
    - name: Run the rollback tasks
      ansible.builtin.import_role:
        name: cgroupv2
        tasks_from: rollback.yml
      tags: [rollback]
